            <ArticleTitle>A novel clinical course of free-floating left atrial ball thrombus without mitral stenosis treated by anticoagulants.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>297-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jjcc.2008.11.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Free-floating left atrial ball thrombus is rare. We describe a case of a 48-year-old man who had free-floating left atrial ball thrombus that was not accompanied by mitral stenosis and that was treated aggressively with anticoagulants. Echocardiography revealed dramatic disappearance of the thrombus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
